    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract interface of a meshfree kernel (window) function <formula id="46">$ \phi_A(\boldsymbol{x}) $</formula>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A kernel function is attached to a node (particle) <formula id="9">$ A $</formula> with center <formula id="47">$ \boldsymbol{x}_A $</formula> and has compact support. The reproducing kernel approximation (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_reproducing_kernel_approximation" kindref="compound">ReproducingKernelApproximation</ref>) builds its shape functions <formula id="48">$ \Psi_A $</formula> by correcting these kernels such that polynomials up to a given order are reproduced exactly; the continuity of <formula id="48">$ \Psi_A $</formula> is inherited from the kernel.</para>
<para>All coordinates are passed as raw arrays of length <formula id="49">$ d $</formula> (the spatial dimension of the kernel). The configuration in which the coordinates are given (reference or current) is decided by the caller; the kernel only compares them with its center coordinates. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
